    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1315">

                <pb facs="1072" n="1062" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1062"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.7146/2–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-11T16:00:00+08:00">February 11,
                            1949—4 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 12—12:35 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Informed last night by intermediary, who stated categorically he transmitted
                    message “in personal capacity” as local Foreign Office branch now defunct, that
                    Communist authorities gave oral approval continued use Consular radio for
                    present, permission without prejudice question later delivery over of station.
                    Since my position regarding handing over Government property already set forth
                    (see Consular reference telegram<anchor n="37" xml:id="d1315-f1"/>), did not
                    consider it appropriate or desirable argue possible later Communist demand
                    now.</p>
                <p>Consul General ceased accept press messages effective time Communist occupation
                    Peiping and early issued office order directing care regarding character message
                    sent plain, aim being avoidance giving Communists ground protest. Recommend no
                    publicity.</p>
                <p>Repeated Nanking 176, Shanghai 181.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
